        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": ">using set foldmethod=indent is close enough\n\nI really don't think it is. For me what indentscope shows vs what `indent` folds is vastly different. `indent` also has very strange behavior on comments.\n\nThese are my settings, you can play around with it yourself and see the large disconnect. This is very jarring when editing...\n\n```lua\n            require(\"mini.indentscope\").setup({\n                draw = { delay = 0, priority = 2 },\n                options = { border = \"top\", indent_at_cursor = true, try_as_border = true },\n                symbol = \"│\",\n            })\n```",
            "created_at": "2025-10-16T18:30:17Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/296#issuecomment-3412278586",
            "id": 3412278586,
